! Test v0.93.0: water wB97X-D / STO-3G + C-PCM(water) optimization
! followed by SOLVATED frequencies -- the PCM + freq capability of
! v0.93.0 (semi-numerical: central differences of the PCM-aware
! analytical gradients; the cavity is rebuilt at every displaced
! geometry, i.e. the frequencies are second derivatives of the
! equilibrium-PCM energy surface).
!
! Reference (1 thread, reference netlib BLAS/LAPACK):
!   Final energy: -75.321150034933 Ha   (5 optimization steps;
!                  identical to test_v092 -- the same PCM optimum)
!   Modes: 2039.05 / 3731.32 / 3955.47 cm^-1  (all real)
! Gas-phase wB97X-D modes at the gas optimum for contrast:
!   2042.03 / 3700.56 / 3923.41 cm^-1.
!
! Validation behind this release (BENCHMARK_NOTES_v0.93.0.md): with
! %eps 1.00001 the PCM-aware Hessian reproduces the gas-phase
! frequencies of the same geometry EXACTLY at print precision
! (1790.90 / 4356.65 / 4682.34 cm^-1, B3LYP water) -- the machinery
! collapses to gas physics when solvation vanishes.
%method  WB97X-D
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt+freq
%pcm     cpcm
%solvent water
%charge  0
%mult    1
%geom angstrom
O 0 0 0.1173
H 0 0.7572 -0.4692
H 0 -0.7572 -0.4692
*end
